1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.540
Materials discovery can now imagine millions of crystals.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.770
Google DeepMind's GNoME proposed 2.2 million.

3
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:14.760
But by late 2023, only 736 had been independently synthesized.

4
00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:17.410
The scarce resource is no longer prediction.

5
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:18.770
It is trust.

6
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.730
Every stage leaks.

7
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.220
Generators omit complex material classes.

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:31.300
Universal machine-learned potentials are least reliable at surfaces, vacancies, and defects.

9
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.540
And laboratories inherit every upstream error.

10
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:39.230
More activity does not automatically produce more validated materials.

11
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.900
The correction layer sits between prediction and synthesis.

12
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:54.110
It measures a predictor's systematic error as a physical field over local atomic environments, corrects that error at runtime, and proves which claims remain inside the evidence boundary.

13
00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:57.480
The field is fixed by three standard observables.

14
00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.230
A fourth surface is held back as a blind test.

15
00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:12.440
Across 36 model-and-material combinations, predicted and measured errors correlate at zero point nine oh six, with zero adjustable parameters.

16
00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:18.320
Quantitative claims are then sealed as Lean 4 theorems with hash-locked provenance.

17
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:23.220
The machine-generated proof inventory records zero unfinished proofs.

18
00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.920
It once rejected a rounded success count, changing 27 improvements to 26.

19
00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:33.160
Trust means being able to say no to yourself.

20
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:39.860
The correction deploys beside existing CHGNet or MACE calculators as a LAMMPS overlay.

21
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.990
In Python, measured overhead is 15.6 percent.

22
00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:51.240
On a blind nickel surface, relative error fell from 9.7 percent to 1.5 percent.

23
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:53.330
Users keep their simulators.

24
00:01:53.630 --> 00:01:55.850
The correction makes them more trustworthy.

25
00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:59.220
The investment is not a bet on one material.

26
00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.010
It is infrastructure for every materials-discovery program.

27
00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:13.760
Generators, databases, autonomous labs, manufacturers, and national labs keep their own tools while gaining a shared correction-and-verification layer.

28
00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.790
The face-centered-cubic field is established.

29
00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:23.610
Other structure families and industrial validation remain open work, with explicit go-or-no-go gates.

30
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.130
That honesty is the product.

31
00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:29.410
The world does not need more predicted crystals.

32
00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.163
It needs predictions laboratories can act on.
